files: maid.glb (model/gltf-binary), maid.generated_image_url.jpeg (image/jpeg)
each file lands in your folder under its name, and its `fetched:` line names its /cdn/ address, the one the world uses. With no `fetched:` line below, `spawn tripo status 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6 --out maid.glb` lands them.
facing: a workshop file, so it faces the way its bytes do: Tripo puts the side that maid.generated_image_url.jpeg shows on +X. Set model.forward to where the subject faces there: toward you "+x", away "-x", to the picture's left "+z", to its right no forward.
next: `spawn tripo texture 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6`, `spawn tripo segment 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6`, `spawn tripo rig 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6`, `spawn tripo retopo 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6 --face_limit <n>` or `spawn tripo convert 5d1c97ad-920c-4bc7-9a14-685351d7d7c6 --format FBX` take this task by its id; finish by hand in Blender.
